[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte ceramic bowls filled with parmesan and pistachio olive oil popcorn, centered in the frame with generous negative space to accommodate a circular crop. Shot from a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component is visible with a shallow depth of field that keeps the foreground bowl sharp and the secondary bowl softly blurred in the background. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left highlights the textures, creating a slight, authentic sheen on the olive oil-coated kernels. The surface is a warm, aged oak table with visible grain and a few scattered crumbs. The popcorn is light, fluffy, and golden-white, generously dusted with finely grated parmesan cheese that clings to the crevices. Roughly chopped green pistachios are integrated naturally throughout the popcorn mix, along with tiny, visible flecks of dried thyme and black pepper. A vintage wooden spoon rests casually beside the foreground bowl. The styling is lived-in and authentic, reflecting a homemade snack for two. Small traces of the preparation are visible: a stray pistachio shard and a few grains of thyme on the wooden surface. The atmosphere is warm, golden-hour, and cozy. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
